				942,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Wind): Regenerate tsconfig.tsbuildinfo with updated build metadata\n\nThe TypeScript incremental build metadata file was regenerated after module resolution changes in the project. The tsbuildinfo grew from ~317KB to ~1MB reflecting updated program structure and declaration maps.\n\nThis is an automated build artifact update with no impact on public API or runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "b37a6426c05c64149902b7f88a73711d4914ff52"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:08:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				942,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add per-subsystem IPC routing tiers to Tier utility\n\nIntroduce 14 new type definitions and their corresponding Tier object entries in `Source/Utility/Tier.ts` for per-subsystem routing, mirroring Cocoon's routing tiers: Terminal, SCM, Debug, LanguageFeatures, Search, OutputChannel, NativeHost, TreeView, Storage, Model, Tasks, Auth, Encryption, ExtensionHost, and WebSocket.\n\nEach subsystem gets its own union type (e.g. TierTerminalValue = \"Mountain\" | \"Node\") and a Tier entry with a static default that matches the values in `.env.Land` and `Mountain/build.rs::EmitTierDefaults`. The ExtensionHost and WebSocket tiers use distinct value sets (Process/WebWorker/Disabled and Disabled/Mountain/Mist respectively) reflecting their unique routing semantics.\n\nThis enables the Wind service layer to resolve per-subsystem IPC routing at runtime rather than relying on a single global IPC tier, laying the groundwork for fine-grained traffic splitting between Mountain native backend and Cocoon Node host.",
			"SHA": "0e75c857c75fa3f13588635bb43243dc3f7b16a7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T13:47:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡏⠀⠀⠀",
				942,
				300
			],
			"Message": "chore(Wind): Remove stale generated bridge shapes and service catalogs\n\nDelete the entire set of generated TypeScript artifacts under Source/Effect/, including the CommandCatalog, ServiceCatalog, all ~500 IAsteriskUpstream service interface definitions, and all 16 bridge shape implementations (UserSettings, WorkbenchActivity, WorkbenchClipboard, etc.).\n\nThese files were produced by the upstream code generation pipeline and have been superseded by regenerated versions in subsequent daily refresh cycles. Retaining them adds noise to the source tree and risks stale definitions being consumed by the build system.\n\nNo functional changes — the deletion removes only generated artifacts with no hand-authored code.",
			"SHA": "1c36744bf75c2bb85b02f4c951361e33ed3dab32"
		},
		{
